course: dictionary
lesson: 468
title: Arrange: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Arrange is a verb, which means an action word. It changes to arrange, arranges, arranged and arranging. Its main meaning is to put things in a neat or useful order or position. «She arranged the books by colour» tells you the books were placed in a set order.
explain: Arrange can also mean to plan something so it happens, like a meeting or a party. «Mum arranged a playdate for Saturday» means she made the plan. The words around the word show which meaning is used.
explain: In music, to arrange a piece means to change it so different instruments or voices can play it. When you meet arrange, read the nearby words: books and flowers point to putting in order, a time or place points to planning, and instruments or voices point to music.
fact: Arrange means to put things in a neat or useful order or position, or to plan something so it happens.
fact: «Arranged» can show a plan: a meeting, a party or a lift has been arranged when someone has made it happen.
fact: In maths, you arrange numbers from smallest to largest, or objects in rows and columns.
fact: «They arranged watches» means they took turns to stay awake, with one person sleeping in Toad's room at night.
fact: Dmitri Mendeleev arranged the elements into the periodic table. He left gaps for elements not yet found, predicted them, and they were found later.
exercise: «She arranged the flowers in a vase on the table.» What does arranged mean here? | To forget them | To break the vase | *To put them in a neat position | To throw them away
exercise: Ben says, «Let's arrange to meet at the park at five.» What does arrange mean? | To sing a song | *To plan a meeting so it happens | To rearrange the furniture | To hide from everyone
exercise: Numbers can be put into order. Find and copy one word that means to put things into order. | *arrange | smallest | largest | numbers
test: «Mendeleev arranged the elements into a table, leaving gaps.» What does arranged mean? | Broke apart | Painted | *Put into a planned order | Mixed up
test: In «They arranged watches», what does arranged mean? | Painted the watches | Lost the watches | *Planned turns, so one person was always on watch | Sold the watches
exam: «The band arranged the old song for a choir.» Which meaning of arranged fits? | Shouted the song loudly | Stopped the music at once | *Changed the song so a choir can sing it | Forgot the words of the song
